  "description": "Re-runs fr_pullback_k3_test under the CORRECTED (self-normalized) q-Plancherel measure, closing the question the 2026-09-04 convention-gap audit left open. Self-normalizing is exactly the substitution [n]_q! -> c_n*[n]_q!, so this patches the k3 module's qfac and re-runs its own functions unmodified -- same braid words, same upstream chi witnesses, same functional. Checks three things: that the unpatched run reproduces the committed figures; that the scaling law (ratio scales by c_n) holds on the FR weights and not merely the uniform ones; and whether the knot RANKING and the PARTIAL-support verdict survive. Note the k3 test computes chi in float64 (q_f64 = float(Q0)); that ~1e-16 defect is separate, far below the ~53% normalization effect, and is NOT addressed here.",
